Changes in this copy:
- pages/blocked.html and pages/challenge.html: footer text changed.
- corvus/rules.lua, corvus/challenge.lua, corvus/login.lua: the signing and status
  keys are read from /data/sentinel/secrets.json instead of environment variables,
  and refused requests are flagged for the traffic counters.
- corvus/traffic.lua, corvus/host.lua, corvus/hostlog.lua, corvus/verify.lua and the
  corvus/status-*.lua entry points are new (Nginx Proxy Manager). traffic.lua replaces
  the Corvus access-log traffic collector for the automatic "under attack" mode.
- The backend code that writes their configuration (backend/lib/sentinel/) is a
  JavaScript port of parts of the Corvus control plane (Go), under the same license.

Country lookups can use IP-to-country data from DB-IP (https://db-ip.com), licensed
under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). It is downloaded at runtime only
when a security rule uses a country condition.
